{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/198600-giant-and-huge-size-and-how-they-work-together","id":198600,"title":"Giant and Huge Size and how they work together?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-15T23:34:09-07:00","id":198600,"title":"Giant and Huge Size and how they work together?","content":"One of my players posed an interesting question to me. As we're not using the &quot;simplified merits&quot; rules in our Demon game it means that physical merits, such as Giant, are attached to a Cover and not the demon in his true Demonic Form. At a glance this is fine, after all, there is a Demonic Form modification called Huge Size which increases the Demon's size category by 4. (Turning a static Size 5 demonic form into a Size 9 demonic form.)<br /> <br /> However the interesting nature of this suggests that one could spend merit dots when building a patchwork cover to give that cover the Giant merit. Then when assuming partial transformation they could then increase that size by 4 on top of that provided by the Giant merit.<br /> <br /> This means that if a Demon's cover has Giant then their size is 6. If they then activate partial transformation and take Huge Size they then become size 10. This is larger than they are actually when fully transformed, as they are size 9 when in Full Transformation.<br /> <br /> An interesting conundrum, I feel. On one hand I want to say that this is fine - as it's the equivalent of messing with reality by adding &quot;I'm really big&quot; as a cosmic factor and thus being able to &quot;stack&quot; the &quot;big&quot; on your human form and create a new outcome. This kind of bizarre interplay with reality is a day in life of a demon. However, mechanically, it seems strange because it means that a player cannot take the Giant merit for their Demonic Form in addition to Huge Size and so can't be that big on their own.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T23:41:07-07:00","id":198617,"title":"","content":"It depends. The Giant merit <i>can</i> be applied directly to a demonic form(after all, not all physical merits, or merits in general, relate to human covers), let's establish that. That's not just a simplified merits thing. A demon can have Ambidexterity for his demonic form, and all that other good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T00:03:35-07:00","id":198633,"title":"","content":"OK! Thank you for that clarification, ArcaneArts. I had supposed that <i>should</i> be the case but I'm glad to hear it from someone much more experienced than myself. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:05:06-07:00","id":199008,"title":"","content":"Not even Demon form, as I understood, a merit can be a part of demon himself, for example the said Ambidextrous could be a demons thing available in all covers.. of course, some clumsy guy instantly becoming ambidextrous is easily a Compromise (if the guy signed a pact and thus, became a cover for a demon) so he most likely uses it only in covers which might have it or hide it unless he needs it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T11:47:16-07:00","id":202303,"title":"","content":"It's really only Social Merits that are different between Covers. Unless you use the simplified rules. Most other Merits always apply, such as Large Size. Unless the Demon doesn't want that to apply to her Cover; I see no problem with being selective about it, as long as the choice is consistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}